# Enum Guardrail Rule

## CRITICAL: Enum Usage Requirements

All enum values in this codebase MUST be imported from `@/lib/enums.ts`.
NEVER use raw string literals for enum values.

## Forbidden Patterns

The following string literals are BANNED and must NEVER appear:

```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Will cause runtime errors
"VIEW_DOWNLOAD"
"VIEW_ANNOTATE" 
"FULL"
"EMAIL"
"CASE_ACCESS"
```

## Required Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Import and use enum members
import { AccessLevel, ShareType, UserRole } from "@/lib/enums";

// Access levels
if (accessLevel === AccessLevel.VIEW) { }
if (accessLevel === AccessLevel.COMMENT) { }
if (accessLevel === AccessLevel.EDIT) { }

// Share types
if (shareType === ShareType.USER) { }
if (shareType === ShareType.ORGANIZATION) { }

// User roles
if (user.role === UserRole.ADMIN) { }
if (user.role === UserRole.COURT_REPORTER) { }
```

## Migration Reference

| Deprecated Value | New Enum Member |
|-----------------|-----------------|
| VIEW_DOWNLOAD | AccessLevel.VIEW |
| VIEW_ANNOTATE | AccessLevel.COMMENT |
| FULL | AccessLevel.EDIT |
| EMAIL | ShareType.USER |
| CASE_ACCESS | ShareType.ORGANIZATION |

## Type Safety

When creating objects with enum fields:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
const share: TranscriptShare = {
  accessLevel: AccessLevel.COMMENT,
  shareType: ShareType.USER,
};

// ❌ WRONG - String literal
const share = {
  accessLevel: "COMMENT",  // Bad!
  shareType: "USER",       // Bad!
};
```

## Validation Functions

Use the helper functions in `@/lib/enums.ts`:

```typescript
import { isValidEnumValue, parseEnum, AccessLevel } from "@/lib/enums";

// Validate user input
if (isValidEnumValue(AccessLevel, userInput)) {
  // Safe to use
}

// Parse with fallback
const level = parseEnum(AccessLevel, userInput, AccessLevel.VIEW);
```
